Initial conditions for the AGORA simulation presented in Roca-Fabrega et al. 2021.
The initial conditions were generated by MUSIC (music.conf) in the AREPO format
(agora_arepo.hdf5) and then converted into SWIFT compatible ICs
(agora_swift.hdf5) with the python3 script convert_ic.py. The run.sh script
downloads the converted ICs; to regenerate them, run MUSIC with music.conf and
then python3 convert_ic.py.
We use SWIFT to cancel the h- and a-factors from the ICs.

The IC consists in a halo evolving to a virial mass of ∼ 1e12 Msun at z = 0 with a relatively
quiescent merger history between z = 2 and 0. The cosmological parameters are taken from WMAP7/9+SNe+BAO.
The target halo contains the highest-resolution dark matter particles of masses = 2.8e5 Msun.

To run this example, SWIFT must be configured with the following options:

./configure --with-subgrid=GEAR --with-grackle=/path/to/grackle